From: osy <osy@turing.llc>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 21:08:37 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] virtio-gpu: retire fences immediately when the renderer
 context is dead
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

virgl_renderer_context_create_fence fails when the proxy render worker
has died (crashed mid-teardown); the fence was silently dropped, never
signaled, and the guest GPU scheduler eventually bugchecked
(VIDEO_TDR_FAILURE) waiting on it.  Respond OK right away instead —
the cmd is not on fenceq yet at this point, so the response both
signals the fence and keeps it off the queue.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5

(cherry picked from utmapp/qemu commit a0f453befd; ui/console API renamed for 11.1)
---
 hw/display/virtio-gpu-virgl.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/display/virtio-gpu-virgl.c b/hw/display/virtio-gpu-virgl.c
index 5071f3f1bc6..643756b1307 100644
--- a/hw/display/virtio-gpu-virgl.c
+++ b/hw/display/virtio-gpu-virgl.c
@@ -1232,6 +1232,15 @@ void virtio_gpu_virgl_process_cmd(VirtIOGPU *g,
             qemu_log_mask(LOG_GUEST_ERROR,
                           "%s: virgl_renderer_context_create_fence error: %s",
                           __func__, strerror(-ret));
+            /*
+             * The renderer context is gone (e.g. its render-server worker
+             * died mid-teardown): this fence can never retire through the
+             * timeline.  Complete it now; the cmd is not on fenceq yet, so
+             * responding both signals the fence and keeps it off the queue.
+             * Leaving it pending wedges the guest's GPU scheduler
+             * (VIDEO_TDR_FAILURE bugcheck on Windows).
+             */
+            virtio_gpu_ctrl_response_nodata(g, cmd, VIRTIO_GPU_RESP_OK_NODATA);
         }
         return;
     }
